// array_new_jagged_quest2.tk -- `new T[n][]?` is the allocator's spelling of
// `T[]?[]`, a row that may be null (D101). A SECOND `?` over it would be a
// nullable of a nullable, which teko does not have -- the same refusal the
// type position gives `T[]? ?`, now reachable through the allocator too.
// (Written with a blank: `??` on its own is the null-coalescing token, D45.)

// expect-refuse: teko: a nullable of a nullable is not taught
// expect-refuse-line: 11

i64 main() {
    i64[]?[] m = new i64[2][]? ?;
    return 0;
}
